      "moduleType": "demo",
      "prefab": "demoPrefab",
      "moduleName": "Fundamental Electron-Domain Geometries",
      "description": "Explore the five basic spatial arrangements that minimize electron domain repulsion around a central atom.",
      "author": "Dr. Evelyn Vance",
      "institution": "University of Chemical Sciences",
      "dateCreated": "2023-10-15",
      "educationalObjectives": [
        "Identify the 5 primary electron-domain arrangements",
        "Correlate the number of electron domains (2 to 6) with idealized bond angles"
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Observe the 3D arrangements of electron clouds around the central atom as the domains increase.",
        "Note how electrostatic repulsion forces the domains as far apart as possible."
      ],
